      },
      "worked": "The perimeter consists of the arc and two radii:\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=r\\theta+2r\\\\P&=r(\\theta+2)\\\\r&=\\frac{P}{\\theta+2}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor a nondegenerate sector, $0<\\theta<2\\pi$, so\n$$2<\\theta+2<2\\pi+2.$$\nTaking reciprocals reverses the inequalities because all quantities are positive:\n$$\\frac{1}{2\\pi+2}<\\frac{1}{\\theta+2}<\\frac{1}{2}.$$\nMultiplying by $P>0$ gives\n$$\\frac{P}{2(\\pi+1)}<r<\\frac{P}{2}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
